{"id":"GHSA-9wg5-mj3p-v49q","axis":"advisories","repo":"digitalbazaar/forge","sha":"c7f42614d5166a77ddf11ce174b2601b14f6956b","parsed":{"files":[{"path":"CHANGELOG.md","lines":["@@ -150,6 +150,18 @@ Forge ChangeLog","   - Reported by wzc.","   - CVE ID: [CVE-TBD]()","   - GHSA ID: [GHSA-4642-5mcj-2rqw](https://github.com/digitalbazaar/forge/security/advisories/GHSA-4642-5mcj-2rqw)","+- **LOW**: Certificate signature verified with the issuer's signature scheme.","+  - An Improper Verification of Cryptographic Signature (CWE-347)","+    vulnerability in node-forge versions 1.4.0 and below lets a certificate","+    labeled as signed with RSASSA-PSS pass chain verification with a PKCS#1","+    v1.5 signature. `certificate.verify(child)` and `verifyCertificateChain()`","+    chose the RSA padding scheme and PSS parameters from the issuer","+    certificate instead of the child certificate. The signature must still","+    be made with the issuer's key, so this only misleads applications that","+    rely on a certificate's signature algorithm.","+  - Reported by Brian Lee (Georgia Tech SSLab, Team Atlanta).","+  - CVE ID: [CVE-TBD]()","+  - GHSA ID: [GHSA-9wg5-mj3p-v49q](https://github.com/digitalbazaar/forge/security/advisories/GHSA-9wg5-mj3p-v49q)"," "," ### Fixed"," - [rsa] Require a canonical DER DigestInfo in RSASSA PKCS#1 v1.5 signature","@@ -190,6 +202,10 @@ Forge ChangeLog","   parsed as `basicConstraints`."," - [x509] Enforce `basicConstraints` `pathLenConstraint` in chain verification","   for CA certificates without a `keyUsage` extension.","+- [x509] Verify a certificate's signature with the padding scheme and","+  parameters of its own signature algorithm, using the issuer's public key.","+  PKCS#1 v1.5 certificates issued by an RSASSA-PSS certificate, and the","+  reverse, failed verification before."," "," ## 1.4.0 - 2026-03-24"," "],"additions":16,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"lib/x509.js","lines":["@@ -727,12 +727,14 @@ var _createSignatureDige